module

public import CFSG.Quasithin.Chapter1.Section03.Embeddings.InvariantThree.SporadicActions.J4.PairActions.Coverage.FixedTwoSubgroup.Elementary.InvolutionAbsorption.QuotientIncidence.PairOrder

/-!
# Concrete matrix conditions for max2 reducibility

The actual max2 two-core quotient is the group generated by the certified
12-dimensional binary matrices. Its three-core is characteristic without any
recognition hypothesis. The remaining structural calculation must give this
three-core order three and put it inside every elementary-nine subgroup
permuting with a Sylow two-subgroup. The other source alternative has order
27; its permuting product would have order 6912 in this same matrix group.

The conditions below are outstanding finite-group calculations, not asserted
results. They mention neither actors nor invariant Frattini subgroups. The
assembly in the parent module retains responsibility for proving them.

Source: Aschbacher–Smith, proof of Proposition 1.3.4, printed p.511/PDF p.528
of `refs/quasithin.pdf`; GLS3 Table 5.3i and the certified matrix quotient.
-/

@[expose] public section
open Subgroup
open scoped Pointwise
open Janko4.OuterReduction.FixedGenerator.NormalizerSquares.TwoCoreCentralizerData

namespace CFSG.Quasithin.Chapter1.XiEmbedding.InvariantThree.SporadicActions.J4Reduction.Adequate.Max2

/-- The actual quotient matrix carrier, without an abstract family tag. -/
abbrev MatrixGroup := LowerBound.quotientSubgroup

/-- Containment in the complement itself, not merely in the pair product. -/
def ElementaryCubicContainment : Prop :=
  ∀ (S : Sylow 2 MatrixGroup) (R : Subgroup MatrixGroup),
    IsElementaryAbelian 3 R → Nat.card R = 9 →
    (R : Set MatrixGroup) * (S : Set MatrixGroup) =
      (S : Set MatrixGroup) * (R : Set MatrixGroup) → pCore 3 MatrixGroup ≤ R

/-- The finite order exclusion sufficient for the extraspecial source branch. -/
def Order27Exclusion : Prop :=
  ∀ K : Subgroup MatrixGroup, Nat.card K ≠ 6912

end CFSG.Quasithin.Chapter1.XiEmbedding.InvariantThree.SporadicActions.J4Reduction.Adequate.Max2
